    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a volatile slate today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (74.74) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). Despite facing the formidable Gerrit Cole, **Gunnar Henderson** remains an elite play; his projection is bolstered by a significant +16% park adjustment and +14% platoon advantage, proving that his underlying power metrics can transcend even the most difficult SP_xERA matchups. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in an ideal spot against Kyle Bradish, benefiting from a favorable home park and a potent #3 spot in the lineup. **Sam Antonacci** also ranks as a standout, leveraging a +10% order bonus and strong SP matchup against Grant Holmes to secure a high-efficiency start.\n\nThe benching of **Nasim Nunez** (36.77) serves as the most difficult decision of the day. While **Nasim Nunez** is a primary weapon for our Stolen Base requirements, his projected output was severely capped by a difficult matchup against Jacob deGrom and a suboptimal #9 spot in the lineup. The optimizer prioritized the consistency of **Drake Baldwin** (64.69), who benefits from a high-floor #2 order slot and a neutral matchup against Anthony Kay. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who remains on the IL, while keeping an eye on **Heliot Ramos** (64.75), who earns a start despite a slight drag from SB-suppressing opposing catchers.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Liam Hicks** (54.32) and **Coby Mayo** (45.87). **Coby Mayo** is currently skating on the edge of our efficiency floor; any downward shift in his lineup position or late-breaking weather patterns at the stadium could render him a liability. While we are missing the presence of **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.** due to scheduling, the active roster\u2014including **Miguel Vargas**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Dominic Smith**\u2014is well-positioned to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings, provided we avoid excessive exposure to elite arms like deGrom and Cole.",
